-- Core retire and dispatch events, relative to the middle's scope (TOP.NzeaCore.core.middle).
--
-- These are the events the retire counters cannot answer: the counters say how many, these say when and in what order.
-- Bind them with --event, e.g. the commit log with its redirects marked:
--   pulse property --event nzea_core/src/middle/retire.pulse <MIDDLE> Core \
--       --eval 'Core.commit_fire || Core.redirect' --cycles 0-500

-- One instruction retired: register write-back, CSR write and the commit trace all ride this pulse.
commit_fire = commit_valid

-- A taken branch: the backend resolved a redirect and the front restarts from report_redirect_target. The baseline
-- predicts not-taken, so a taken branch is also a mispredict.
redirect = report_flush

-- There is an instruction in the middle: the uop in the execute slot, or a payload still waiting for its operands.
inflight = exValid | decValid

-- A uop enters the execute slot. That is the cycle the read resolved its operands, and the cycle before the backend
-- first sees it.
uop_issue = move

-- The payload could move and does not: the execute slot is free, so what holds it is its own operands — it reads the
-- very instruction that is finishing below it, and the write it waits for lands a cycle later.
operand_wait = decValid & !move & (!exValid | report_complete) & !report_flush
